Foresight's launch checklist, checked against the system

Before anyone relies on it
  yes      the brief names decision, baseline and sign-off
  yes      the table is refused if an expectation fails
  yes      leakage checks run on every training job
  yes      the model's card sits beside it in the registry
  yes      a person promoted it, and wrote down why
  no       a version to roll back to is in the registry

The night it runs alone
  yes      the job refuses a stale warehouse
  yes      a second run does nothing
  yes      the job's rows match the API's (skew test)
  yes      the API refuses a malformed request
  yes      with no model, the rule answers

Once it is live
  yes      alert thresholds are constants, not tuned later
  yes      a holdout is drawn after every list
  no       a failed run alerts a person by the morning
  by hand  the CI gate blocks a worse model (make test)
  by hand  someone who did not build it ran make demo
  by hand  the account team knows 'held out' means no call
  by hand  an owner is named for each part

18 lines: 12 yes, 2 no, 4 by hand
